@page "/docs"
@* "/" is routed here too until the marketing home page lands - then drop this line. *@
@page "/"
<PageTitle>Introduction - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-3">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Introduction</h1>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">Blazor</BzBadge>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">Tailwind v4</BzBadge>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">.NET 10</BzBadge>
        </div>
        <p class="max-w-3xl">Blaizio is a component system for Blazor built as <b>two layers with one rule</b>: behaviour is a package, styling is your source. Headless primitives handle the hard parts - accessibility, keyboard, focus, state - while the styled components are Tailwind files the CLI copies <em>into your project</em>, where you can open, read and change every line.</p>
    </header>

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">The two layers</h2>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div class="rounded-xl border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                    <div class="text-sm font-semibold">Blaizio.Base</div>
                    <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">NuGet</BzBadge>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Headless primitives: correct elements, ARIA roles, keyboard and focus behaviour, and a <code>data-state</code> attribute contract. Zero CSS - style it with anything, or don't take the styled layer at all. <a class="font-medium text-foreground underline underline-offset-4" href="docs/base">Read the Base guide</a>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                    <div class="text-sm font-semibold">Styled components</div>
                    <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">your source</BzBadge>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Tailwind-dressed <code>Bz*</code> components copied in by <a class="font-medium text-foreground underline underline-offset-4" href="docs/cli">the CLI</a> - rewritten to your namespace, tracked for <code>add --diff</code>/<code>--update</code>, never hidden inside a package. Eight skins, color presets, dark mode and RTL included.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Quick start</h2>
        <p>Install the CLI once - <CmdChip Command="dotnet tool install -g Blaizio.Cli" /> - then from your Blazor project:</p>
        <CodeBlock Snippet="Installation/InitExisting" />
        <p>That's a working setup: packages installed, theme CSS written, Tailwind pipeline wired (a Node-free <b>standalone</b> mode is the default), host page patched, and four components in your source tree. The full walkthrough - new apps, existing apps, Base-only - lives on the <a href="docs/installation">Installation page</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">What you get</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>60+ components</b> - from buttons to combo boxes, data tables, command palettes, charts and a sortable tree. Every page has a copy-paste usage block and a live demo.</li>
            <li><b>Accessibility as a baseline</b> - roles, keyboard behaviour and focus management live in the primitive, so they survive any restyling you do.</li>
            <li><b>Theming that composes</b> - eight skins (inlined into the components you install), color presets, chart palettes, radius scales, real webfonts and dark mode - your whole look lives in one tokens file plus your component source, previewable live on <a href="themes">Themes</a>.</li>
            <li><b>A real CLI</b> - <code>new</code>, <code>add</code> (with <code>--diff</code>/<code>--update</code>), <code>apply</code>, <code>remove</code>, <code>uninstall</code>: everything is tracked in <code>blaizio.json</code> and undoable by record.</li>
            <li><b>RTL out of the box</b> - logical properties throughout; flip <code>dir</code> and the components follow. See <a href="docs/direction">Direction</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Where next</h2>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <a href="docs/installation" class="rounded-xl border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground transition-colors hover:border-primary/50">
                <div class="text-sm font-semibold">Installation</div>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Prerequisites and both setup paths, step by step.</p>
            </a>
            <a href="docs/components" class="rounded-xl border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground transition-colors hover:border-primary/50">
                <div class="text-sm font-semibold">Components</div>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">The gallery - demos, usage and API for every component.</p>
            </a>
            <a href="themes" class="rounded-xl border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground transition-colors hover:border-primary/50">
                <div class="text-sm font-semibold">Themes</div>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Compose a theme live and ship it as one command.</p>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
